## Context

The red alert of ticket 1543 (`_alert_red` in `scripts/merge-gate.py`, through
`scripts/runtime_notify.py`) runs `notify-send -a idh "main is red" ...` for
real when the harness test suite runs on a machine with a desktop session.
Every test that drives a red after-merge run in a fixture repository puts a
"main is red" popup on the author's screen.

Observed on padme, 2026-11-13 13:43 CET: twelve or more popups at once,
bodies `after-merge run on <12 hex>: the-check`, `... marker-absent`,
`... the-check, real`, `... marker-absent, seco...`. The commit ids exist in
neither the harness nor climate-finance-het: they are tips of pytest fixture
repositories. `the-check` and `marker-absent` are check names from
`tests/test_after_merge.py` and `tests/test_merge_gate.py`.

Reproduction (one passing test, two real `Notify` calls on the session bus,
body `after-merge run on d63967259d96: marker-absent`):

```sh
dbus-monitor --session "interface='org.freedesktop.Notifications',member='Notify'" &
python3 -m pytest tests/test_after_merge.py -k red_run_alerts -q
```

Read in the code, at `7e95e6496`:

- `test_a_red_run_alerts_and_a_green_run_does_not` redirects the alert file
  with `IDH_ALERT_DIR` but sets `PATH="/usr/bin:/bin"` with the comment
  "no notify-send needed". On padme `notify-send` is `/usr/bin/notify-send`,
  so the popup fires.
- The other red-run tests of the two files set neither: the alert file goes
  to the fixture repository's git directory and the popup to the desktop.
- The rate limit does not help: the key is `after-merge-red-<tip>` and each
  fixture has a fresh tip.

Cost so far: the author read the popups as a red `main` of
climate-finance-het ("main has been red for 13 hours") and a session there
ran every gate of that project, all green, before finding the source. The
real alert is now indistinguishable from test noise.

A second observation, same popup: the text names no repository. With
several projects on one desktop, "main is red" plus a short commit id does
not say whose `main`.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Running the harness test suite on a machine with a desktop session
      sends no desktop notification (shown with the `dbus-monitor` command
      above, or a recording stub ahead of `notify-send` on `PATH`).
- [ ] Positive control: a red after-merge run outside the tests still raises
      the popup and writes the alert file.
- [ ] The popup names the repository whose `main` is red.
- [ ] `make check` passes.
